    "field": "Tropical Atlantic climate variability",
    "problem": "Coupled climate models exhibit large biases when simulating the tropical Atlantic, which limits the predictability of regional climate variations like the West African Monsoon, a problem compounded by a lack of observational data.",
    "method": "This editorial describes the Tropical Atlantic Climate Experiment (TACE), which addresses climate model biases by improving the observational database and conducting process studies to enhance understanding of the region's climate system and its variability.",
    "task": "The task is to advance the understanding of Tropical Atlantic variability and coupled climate model biases by analyzing enhanced observational data and process studies from the Tropical Atlantic Climate Experiment (TACE).",
